  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The policy including the NEP, and programmes in place leading to an increase and Productive Employment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Labour Organization (ILO) is working with Mauritius to achieve several key development goals. These include:
&#x2022;	Promoting a Strong Economy: The ILO is supporting efforts to strengthen the manufacturing, agriculture, and financial services sectors. This includes initiatives to improve skills and foster innovation.
&#x2022;	Addressing Aging Population Challenges: The ILO is helping Mauritius to address the challenges posed by an aging population, such as healthcare, social protection, and labor market adjustments.
&#x2022;	Improving Education and Skills: The ILO is working to enhance the quality of education and training, ensuring that young people are equipped with the skills needed to succeed in the modern workforce.
&#x2022;	Creating a More Inclusive Society: The ILO is promoting social protection and gender equality, aiming to create a more inclusive and equitable society.
To achieve these goals, the ILO is collaborating with various stakeholders, including the government, employers, and workers&apos; organizations. Key initiatives include:
&#x2022;	Developing a National Employment Policy: This policy aims to create more jobs, improve skills, and strengthen labor market institutions.
&#x2022;	Supporting Skills Development: The ILO is providing training and support to young people and workers to enhance their skills and employability.
&#x2022;	Promoting Social Protection: The ILO is working to expand social protection coverage to ensure that all workers have access to essential social security benefits.
By working together, the ILO and Mauritius can create a more prosperous and equitable future for all.</narrative>
  </description>
